WEBVTT

00:00:05.350 --> 00:00:06.920
This won't pass.

00:00:06.920 --> 00:00:10.900
The dugout won't switch you out until you take a hit.

00:00:11.560 --> 00:00:13.320
Leave the mound yourself.

00:00:13.320 --> 00:00:14.990
Wh-What?

00:00:15.400 --> 00:00:16.750
Why wouldn't you?

00:00:16.750 --> 00:00:19.460
You can't pitch any strikes, and you can't even throw into my mitt.

00:00:19.460 --> 00:00:23.480
Not to mention you were spacing out on the mound just now.

00:00:24.470 --> 00:00:28.420
Were you doing image training of giving up a hit to Kyoshiro?

00:00:29.370 --> 00:00:31.920
I'm not criticizing you.

00:00:31.920 --> 00:00:35.550
You did more than enough as a starting pitcher.

00:00:35.550 --> 00:00:40.350
If it weren't for the no-no, you would've been off the mound long ago.

00:00:40.820 --> 00:00:42.650
So leave.

00:00:42.650 --> 00:00:44.890
If you aren't obsessed with getting a no-no,

00:00:45.270 --> 00:00:47.770
we can win this game with Watts.

00:00:47.770 --> 00:00:49.730
What's Keene doing?

00:00:49.730 --> 00:00:51.570
What's he saying to him?

00:00:58.890 --> 00:01:00.700
Okay.

00:01:12.590 --> 00:01:14.490
Wh-What is this?

00:01:14.490 --> 00:01:17.010
Shigeno's leaving the mound!

00:01:23.850 --> 00:01:26.270
Wh-What?!

00:01:31.770 --> 00:01:37.070
egaita yume to koko ni aru ima

00:01:31.770 --> 00:01:37.070
I look at my dream and my current reality,

00:01:37.070 --> 00:01:42.370
futatsu no keshiki mikurabete mo

00:01:37.070 --> 00:01:42.370
but no matter how much I compare the two,

00:01:42.370 --> 00:01:47.750
katachi wo kaete koko ni aru no wa

00:01:42.370 --> 00:01:47.750
the only thing I truly have

00:01:47.750 --> 00:01:53.050
tashika na hitotsuno mono

00:01:47.750 --> 00:01:53.050
is the one and only thing I'm sure of.

00:01:53.050 --> 00:01:58.380
sugiyuku haru wo oshiminagara mo

00:01:53.050 --> 00:01:58.380
Even as I bid a sad farewell to spring,

00:01:58.380 --> 00:02:03.640
bokura no maku aketa ano natsu

00:01:58.380 --> 00:02:03.640
the season of the coming summer began.

00:02:03.640 --> 00:02:09.020
ironna koto wo wakari hajimeta

00:02:03.640 --> 00:02:09.020
I had begun to understand many things

00:02:09.020 --> 00:02:15.110
aki to nanika ushinatta fuyu

00:02:09.020 --> 00:02:15.110
by the fall, but I lost something in the winter.

00:02:15.110 --> 00:02:20.660
garakuta no yama kara

00:02:15.110 --> 00:02:20.660
In the junk I've piled up,

00:02:20.660 --> 00:02:24.740
sagasu ano hi no yume

00:02:20.660 --> 00:02:24.740
I search for the dream I had way back when.

00:02:24.740 --> 00:02:30.040
hibike kono koe yo

00:02:24.740 --> 00:02:30.040
Let my voice echo on.

00:02:30.040 --> 00:02:36.300
hibike kono kokoro yo

00:02:30.040 --> 00:02:36.300
Let my heart resonate.

00:02:36.300 --> 00:02:41.970
namida kareru made

00:02:36.300 --> 00:02:41.970
Until my tears dry up,

00:02:41.970 --> 00:02:47.020
mada denu kotae oitsuzukete

00:02:41.970 --> 00:02:47.020
I'll chase the answer I've been searching for.

00:02:47.020 --> 00:02:52.360
namida hareru made

00:02:47.020 --> 00:02:52.360
Until my tears clear away,

00:02:52.360 --> 00:02:57.360
waga yukue mayoi nagara mo

00:02:52.360 --> 00:02:57.360
though I may lose my way,

00:02:57.360 --> 00:03:01.200
egakikake no ima

00:02:57.360 --> 00:03:01.200
I'll continue to paint the present,

00:03:01.200 --> 00:03:02.700
kizamu

00:03:01.200 --> 00:03:08.450
and carve my existence with my own two hands.

00:03:02.700 --> 00:03:03.990
akashi

00:03:03.990 --> 00:03:08.450
kono te de

00:03:09.210 --> 00:03:14.210
In an Impossible Dilemma

00:03:09.210 --> 00:03:14.210
In an Impossible Dilemma

00:03:16.760 --> 00:03:20.810
The third game of the season between the Hornets and the Seagulls has just finished,

00:03:20.810 --> 00:03:24.550
with the famous rookie, Shigeno Goro, making his major league debut.

00:03:25.470 --> 00:03:30.480
Shigeno racked up a bunch of strike outs with his 150 km/h forkballs

00:03:30.480 --> 00:03:33.690
and allowed zero hits through six innings of play.

00:03:33.690 --> 00:03:36.050
He didn't give up any hits in the seventh inning either,

00:03:36.050 --> 00:03:41.030
leading many fans to believe they might see the first no-hitter debut in major league history.

00:03:41.030 --> 00:03:43.880
Whoa! No way.

00:03:43.880 --> 00:03:44.870
However, in the eighth inning,

00:03:45.520 --> 00:03:49.160
the bases were loaded after a teammate's error and two consecutive walks,

00:03:49.160 --> 00:03:54.710
and Shigeno ultimately left the mound after pitching a no-hitter for seven innings and two outs.

00:03:58.100 --> 00:04:01.780
Their closer, Watts, brought the team out of the bind and finished the game.

00:04:01.780 --> 00:04:04.590
The game ended with the Hornets up 2-0,

00:04:05.180 --> 00:04:07.160
giving Shigeno a debut victory.

00:04:07.160 --> 00:04:08.480
Why'd he leave?

00:04:08.480 --> 00:04:11.770
The team's head coach, Stacy, had this to say about the pitching change:

00:04:12.250 --> 00:04:16.230
"It's a shame to see him miss the no-hitter, but it seems that he threw out his back

00:04:16.230 --> 00:04:18.360
and wanted to leave the mound, so I switched him out.

00:04:18.360 --> 00:04:22.740
However, it shouldn't affect any future games."

00:04:22.740 --> 00:04:25.640
Oh, so that's what happened.

00:04:25.640 --> 00:04:26.760
Sis.

00:04:27.710 --> 00:04:29.450
I was worried about him.

00:04:29.450 --> 00:04:35.530
He just fell apart all of a sudden and walked off with his head down.

00:04:35.530 --> 00:04:37.040
I'm glad it wasn't anything serious.

00:04:38.760 --> 00:04:40.880
Now I can sleep in peace.

00:04:40.880 --> 00:04:42.510
Good night.

00:04:42.510 --> 00:04:45.890
G-Good night? Kaoru, what about school?!

00:04:47.820 --> 00:04:53.180
He left the mound due to a sore back when he was just four outs away from a no-hitter?

00:04:53.830 --> 00:04:55.380
Would he really?

00:05:09.870 --> 00:05:12.580
I'm really sorry, Shigeno.

00:05:12.580 --> 00:05:15.500
My error really threw you off your game.

00:05:16.590 --> 00:05:17.350
Nah,

00:05:17.350 --> 00:05:19.390
it wasn't really your fault.

00:05:19.390 --> 00:05:20.660
Don't beat yourself up.

00:05:20.660 --> 00:05:22.380
I-Is that so?

00:05:22.860 --> 00:05:24.550
Hey there, Roy.

00:05:24.550 --> 00:05:27.430
Could we switch seats for a bit?

00:05:27.430 --> 00:05:29.430
Oh, sure.

00:05:33.460 --> 00:05:35.140
Nice pitching.

00:05:35.140 --> 00:05:36.520
Congratulations on your first win.

00:05:38.400 --> 00:05:40.610
W-Well, you know...

00:05:40.610 --> 00:05:44.160
I hear the owner is disappointed that you didn't have a no-no game,

00:05:44.160 --> 00:05:45.860
but you didn't really have a choice with your back.

00:05:46.250 --> 00:05:50.530
It's much more important to get through your first season safely.

00:05:51.540 --> 00:05:52.910
Yeah...

00:06:08.480 --> 00:06:14.020
They lost the three-game series against the Jets with only one win,

00:06:14.020 --> 00:06:17.020
and they also lost their first game against the White Hawks.

00:06:17.790 --> 00:06:20.440
He'll be behind right from the start of the season...

00:06:25.530 --> 00:06:27.350
All right, good.

00:06:27.350 --> 00:06:29.270
Is your back feeling okay?

00:06:29.270 --> 00:06:30.280
Yeah.

00:06:30.280 --> 00:06:31.810
All right, good.

00:06:31.810 --> 00:06:34.330
Show us some more of your great pitching today.

00:06:40.010 --> 00:06:41.040
Hey, rookie.

00:06:42.880 --> 00:06:46.800
I'm getting bored from not having any games to pitch in.

00:06:46.800 --> 00:06:50.580
Set up a nice one for me today, okay?

00:07:03.600 --> 00:07:04.600
Hey, Keene.

00:07:05.750 --> 00:07:08.440
What did you think of his pitching the other day?

00:07:09.850 --> 00:07:11.160
What do you mean?

00:07:11.160 --> 00:07:12.690
Don't play dumb with me.

00:07:12.690 --> 00:07:16.120
Even I knew something was up, and I was in the bullpen.

00:07:17.540 --> 00:07:19.100
In that inning,

00:07:19.100 --> 00:07:25.140
he wasn't the same guy who pitched fearlessly at the World Cup.

00:07:25.140 --> 00:07:26.260
Back pain?

00:07:26.260 --> 00:07:28.780
That's just an excuse.

00:07:28.780 --> 00:07:31.140
Hey! What are you saying, Watts?

00:07:31.140 --> 00:07:33.460
He himself said that he hurt his back.

00:07:33.460 --> 00:07:35.870
No, I'm sure he's lying about the pain.

00:07:36.930 --> 00:07:42.800
Besides, Shigeno wouldn't leave the mound with a no-hitter so close

00:07:42.800 --> 00:07:45.110
just because of some pain that would go away after a few days.

00:07:45.110 --> 00:07:46.180
Right?

00:07:46.180 --> 00:07:51.530
No one, not just Shigeno, would give up on getting a no-hitter.

00:07:52.360 --> 00:07:55.020
What are you two talking about?

00:07:55.020 --> 00:07:58.120
He's just a nineteen-year-old rookie.

00:07:58.120 --> 00:08:01.330
It's not surprising that he'd fall apart after focusing so much on the no-hitter,

00:08:01.330 --> 00:08:06.470
and there's nothing wrong with focusing on the team's win.

00:08:07.960 --> 00:08:09.910
We're not saying he did anything wrong.

00:08:10.550 --> 00:08:16.140
It just reminded me of one of my old colleagues, that's all.

00:08:17.470 --> 00:08:22.520
He was also fearless and full of talent, just like Shigeno.

00:08:22.520 --> 00:08:27.140
But he got the yips after a particular error, then retired.

00:08:27.860 --> 00:08:29.320
Y-Yips?

00:08:29.740 --> 00:08:32.190
Wh-What's that?

00:08:32.190 --> 00:08:38.870
The yips is a condition where one loses control of his body due to psychological reasons,

00:08:38.870 --> 00:08:41.410
and it's especially common among athletes.

00:08:42.750 --> 00:08:46.470
He was an infielder and a decent batter,

00:08:46.470 --> 00:08:48.900
but his real skill was his magnificent defense.

00:08:50.640 --> 00:08:52.780
The year he got promoted to the majors,

00:08:52.780 --> 00:08:56.590
he made it to the league championships.

00:08:56.590 --> 00:08:59.850
It was the final game, with the series tied 3-3.

00:09:10.270 --> 00:09:14.950
He made an error that cost his team the victory.

00:09:17.750 --> 00:09:21.790
The media and some of the fans crucified him,

00:09:21.790 --> 00:09:24.540
but no one on the team blamed him for it.

00:09:24.540 --> 00:09:28.460
It seemed like he had moved on,

00:09:28.460 --> 00:09:32.630
but in the first game of the next season...

00:09:41.890 --> 00:09:44.120
He could play just fine in a normal situation,

00:09:44.120 --> 00:09:47.810
but when a game was tied or the score was close,

00:09:47.810 --> 00:09:50.590
he lost his ability to play.

00:09:54.400 --> 00:09:55.980
Get out!

00:09:55.980 --> 00:09:59.400
We can't win if you play, you god of losers!

00:09:59.400 --> 00:10:00.770
Get out of here!

00:10:01.970 --> 00:10:04.180
What in the world has happened to me?

00:10:04.180 --> 00:10:06.910
I was just getting started after finally reaching the majors.

00:10:07.690 --> 00:10:09.400
It wasn't supposed to be like this.

00:10:09.400 --> 00:10:12.090
I... I...

00:10:14.400 --> 00:10:17.620
He did his best by fighting against his yips to remain a major leaguer,

00:10:17.620 --> 00:10:20.290
but he never got over it,

00:10:20.290 --> 00:10:25.260
and ended up leaving the baseball world as if he was being chased out.

00:10:25.260 --> 00:10:29.430
S-So... you're saying what happened to him is happening to Shigeno?

00:10:29.430 --> 00:10:32.690
Well, we don't know that for sure.

00:10:33.960 --> 00:10:35.320
It's just...

00:10:39.150 --> 00:10:43.250
In any case, we'll know more once we see how he pitches today.

00:11:14.580 --> 00:11:18.950
The Hornets are up by three after Keene's three-run homer in the first inning.

00:11:18.950 --> 00:11:24.460
Shigeno had an amazing debut in his first game, leading the team to victory.

00:11:24.460 --> 00:11:27.110
He steps onto the mound today for his second major league game.

00:11:27.110 --> 00:11:30.720
What sort of pitching will he show us today?

00:11:35.010 --> 00:11:36.590
Play ball!

00:11:45.760 --> 00:11:47.050
Strike!

00:11:48.390 --> 00:11:49.580
Great!

00:11:49.580 --> 00:11:52.040
159 km/h right away.

00:11:52.040 --> 00:11:53.360
Thank goodness.

00:11:53.360 --> 00:11:55.450
His back seems to be all right now.

00:12:04.430 --> 00:12:05.380
Out!

00:12:07.060 --> 00:12:07.980
All right!

00:12:07.980 --> 00:12:09.980
The yips my ass!

00:12:09.980 --> 00:12:11.790
He's in great condition.

00:12:11.790 --> 00:12:14.990
He hasn't given up a single hit in the majors yet.

00:12:17.270 --> 00:12:20.310
He might be the real deal.

00:12:20.310 --> 00:12:24.220
You can't be so sure after seeing just his first few pitches.

00:12:24.740 --> 00:12:26.870
Nice pitching, Shigeno!

00:12:30.510 --> 00:12:32.070
You're off to a good start.

00:12:32.070 --> 00:12:34.790
Yeah, I'm glad I am.

00:12:34.790 --> 00:12:40.280
Last game, my body suddenly got heavy in the eighth inning, then my back started hurting.

00:12:40.280 --> 00:12:45.520
The no-no pressure must've tired me out.

00:13:00.330 --> 00:13:01.190
Out!

00:13:03.910 --> 00:13:06.340
Halfway into the fifth, the Hornets are up 5-0.

00:13:06.860 --> 00:13:09.640
And once again, Shigeno has yet to give up a single hit this game!

00:13:09.640 --> 00:13:14.310
Including his previous game, he has pitched eleven consecutive innings with no hits!

00:13:14.310 --> 00:13:16.160
You're doing great, Shigeno!

00:13:16.160 --> 00:13:20.300
Screw the yips. Today's definitely the day to pitch a no-hitter!

00:13:20.300 --> 00:13:23.670
Even if he has the yips, it won't show in this game.

00:13:23.670 --> 00:13:24.440
Huh?

00:13:24.440 --> 00:13:30.030
He was fine pitching in exhibition games when we started off with a big lead,

00:13:30.480 --> 00:13:33.450
since there wasn't any fear of losing the game.

00:13:34.820 --> 00:13:36.500
Hey, that's enough!

00:13:36.500 --> 00:13:40.000
Do you <i>want</i> to see Shigeno with the yips?!

00:13:43.920 --> 00:13:45.630
Safe! Safe!

00:13:46.960 --> 00:13:47.690
A hit!

00:13:47.690 --> 00:13:49.050
It's a hit!

00:13:49.750 --> 00:13:54.680
Shigeno gives up his first major league hit as Victor gets on base with an infield hit!

00:13:55.740 --> 00:13:57.820
So he's finally given up a hit.

00:13:57.820 --> 00:13:59.900
Well, it was bound to happen eventually.

00:13:59.900 --> 00:14:01.470
Don't worry about it, Shigeno!

00:14:01.710 --> 00:14:05.400
Now hitting: number 5, Sylvester!

00:14:04.880 --> 00:14:05.400
Play ball!

00:14:06.280 --> 00:14:08.020
We're up by five runs.

00:14:08.020 --> 00:14:10.440
I don't care about a hit or two.

00:14:10.440 --> 00:14:14.870
The worst thing I could do is load the bases with walks.

00:14:25.730 --> 00:14:28.400
While Shigeno pitched smoothly with no hits until the fourth inning,

00:14:28.400 --> 00:14:32.850
the White Hawks lineup is finally hitting his pitches, with no outs and runners on second and third.

00:14:33.530 --> 00:14:34.420
Goro...

00:14:36.270 --> 00:14:38.440
How was that pitch?

00:14:38.440 --> 00:14:41.190
It was a soft 90 mph fastball.

00:14:41.190 --> 00:14:42.610
90 mph?

00:14:43.050 --> 00:14:44.610
Shigeno...

00:14:45.340 --> 00:14:47.030
This is where things really begin.

00:14:47.030 --> 00:14:51.700
If you can get through this, I'll have to admit that you're the real thing.

00:14:58.890 --> 00:14:59.750
Ball!

00:14:59.750 --> 00:15:03.220
Is it back again?

00:15:03.220 --> 00:15:05.140
We have a giant five run lead!

00:15:13.250 --> 00:15:14.310
Safe!

00:15:19.810 --> 00:15:21.980
T-Time out!

00:15:23.930 --> 00:15:25.480
Hey, Sanders.

00:15:26.270 --> 00:15:27.860
Catch for me.

00:15:27.860 --> 00:15:30.150
I need to warm up my shoulder right away.

00:15:30.150 --> 00:15:31.490
S-Sure.

00:15:35.300 --> 00:15:36.750
What's wrong?

00:15:36.750 --> 00:15:38.830
If you can make it through this inning, you're a winning pitcher.

00:15:39.460 --> 00:15:40.990
Don't rush your pitches.

00:15:40.990 --> 00:15:42.290
I know.

00:15:45.500 --> 00:15:47.730
What's wrong with Shigeno?

00:15:47.730 --> 00:15:50.040
Is his back hurting again?

00:15:50.040 --> 00:15:51.260
Boss,

00:15:51.810 --> 00:15:55.910
there's a chance that we'll lose the lead this inning,

00:15:55.910 --> 00:16:00.230
but can you keep him on the mound until the score is tied?

00:16:00.230 --> 00:16:01.310
What?

00:16:01.670 --> 00:16:03.170
Please.

00:16:03.170 --> 00:16:04.680
What do you mean?

00:16:06.690 --> 00:16:11.660
It's much better for us and for him if we figure this out early.

00:16:13.840 --> 00:16:16.990
Now hitting: number 3, Evans!

00:16:19.980 --> 00:16:25.510
Last game, my body suddenly got heavy in the eighth inning, then my back started hurting.

00:16:27.140 --> 00:16:29.500
If he was serious about that,

00:16:29.500 --> 00:16:32.550
his condition might be more serious than I thought.

00:16:33.400 --> 00:16:36.650
Without him realizing his psychological fear,

00:16:36.650 --> 00:16:40.220
the stress causes his body's motor activities to fail.

00:16:40.990 --> 00:16:44.600
That's a textbook case of the yips.

00:16:45.970 --> 00:16:46.810
Ball.

00:16:49.010 --> 00:16:49.980
Ball.

00:16:49.980 --> 00:16:51.480
Ball two.

00:16:54.030 --> 00:16:56.980
In reality, we should switch him out,

00:16:56.980 --> 00:17:01.120
but if he isn't aware of his own condition, we have to do things the hard way.

00:17:03.830 --> 00:17:06.040
Ball. Ball three.

00:17:10.270 --> 00:17:11.350
What's going on?

00:17:12.140 --> 00:17:14.380
Why do I feel exhausted all of a sudden?

00:17:15.180 --> 00:17:18.080
I can't draw any strength from my body.

00:17:20.170 --> 00:17:21.770
This is serious.

00:17:22.630 --> 00:17:26.900
If his yips is caused by his past mistakes,

00:17:26.900 --> 00:17:31.070
a successful future is the only way to cure it.

00:17:35.800 --> 00:17:37.690
Ball. Ball four!

00:17:38.260 --> 00:17:39.710
This isn't looking good for Shigeno.

00:17:40.190 --> 00:17:43.100
Runners are on first and second after four straight balls, and still no outs.

00:17:43.550 --> 00:17:44.870
Goro...

00:17:44.870 --> 00:17:46.380
What's going on?

00:17:46.380 --> 00:17:47.970
What the hell are you doing?

00:17:47.970 --> 00:17:49.790
You yellow-belly!

00:18:13.490 --> 00:18:14.790
I can't do it.

00:18:14.790 --> 00:18:19.260
If I keep pitching like this, I'm going to bring the team down.

00:18:21.950 --> 00:18:23.340
Hey...

00:18:34.380 --> 00:18:35.580
Wait, Shigeno.

00:18:35.580 --> 00:18:36.920
Where are you going?

00:18:36.920 --> 00:18:37.990
Go back!

00:18:37.990 --> 00:18:39.540
Not today.

00:18:39.540 --> 00:18:42.850
You can go off once you clean up your mess!

00:18:43.850 --> 00:18:45.620
Are you deaf?

00:18:45.620 --> 00:18:46.550
Get back on the mound!

00:18:46.550 --> 00:18:47.560
What?

00:18:47.560 --> 00:18:49.690
What the hell are you saying?

00:18:49.690 --> 00:18:53.040
My body feels like lead and I can't move properly.

00:18:53.040 --> 00:18:54.880
I probably have a fever.

00:18:54.880 --> 00:18:56.880
That's why I can't pitch well.

00:18:56.880 --> 00:18:57.840
Shigeno!

00:18:57.840 --> 00:18:58.780
Hey, what's going on?

00:18:59.200 --> 00:19:03.230
I can't do anything even if I stay on the mound.

00:19:03.230 --> 00:19:04.980
I must have caught a cold!

00:19:04.980 --> 00:19:06.370
Hey, listen, Shigeno!

00:19:06.370 --> 00:19:09.060
Yeah, I'm sorry.

00:19:09.060 --> 00:19:12.120
I shouldn't have slept without a blanket.

00:19:12.120 --> 00:19:16.820
How can I call myself a professional if I can't even manage my health?

00:19:16.820 --> 00:19:18.550
I'll be more careful in the future.

00:19:18.550 --> 00:19:19.390
Shigeno!

00:19:20.630 --> 00:19:21.670
Hey, guys.

00:19:21.670 --> 00:19:22.750
It's about time to...

00:19:22.750 --> 00:19:24.570
I'm sorry. This won't take long.

00:19:25.600 --> 00:19:28.480
Shigeno, I don't care if you're sick.

00:19:29.710 --> 00:19:31.780
If you give up any hits, I'll take responsibility.

00:19:31.780 --> 00:19:33.310
So just get back on the mound.

00:19:34.170 --> 00:19:36.300
You'll take responsibility?

00:19:37.190 --> 00:19:38.880
What are you saying?

00:19:38.880 --> 00:19:41.070
Stop talking nonsense!

00:19:41.470 --> 00:19:46.470
If you walk off now, you'll do the exact same thing in your next game.

00:19:46.470 --> 00:19:49.070
This is for the team, as well as for you.

00:19:49.070 --> 00:19:51.670
We need to figure this out <i>today</i>.

00:19:52.150 --> 00:19:53.410
What?

00:19:53.410 --> 00:19:56.540
Your back hurts? You caught a cold?

00:19:56.540 --> 00:19:58.340
I don't need to hear your lies.

00:19:58.340 --> 00:20:02.840
If you're so afraid of giving up hits, then be a man, tell the truth, and go start over in the minors.

00:20:07.110 --> 00:20:11.270
I'm afraid of giving up hits?

00:20:13.300 --> 00:20:15.110
Hey, I'm losing my patience!

00:20:15.110 --> 00:20:18.460
If this isn't for medical purposes, get back on the field!

00:20:21.450 --> 00:20:24.720
If you don't like what I said, then pull through this situation,

00:20:24.720 --> 00:20:25.820
you coward.

00:20:34.460 --> 00:20:38.160
Keene's taken drastic measures.

00:20:38.160 --> 00:20:40.380
I sure hope this won't backfire.

00:20:41.230 --> 00:20:42.090
Play ball!

00:20:42.090 --> 00:20:43.960
That bastard.

00:20:43.960 --> 00:20:45.500
He better be kidding me.

00:20:45.500 --> 00:20:49.140
I'm running away because I'm afraid of giving up hits?

00:20:49.140 --> 00:20:51.100
I'm a coward?

00:20:51.100 --> 00:20:53.060
Are you kidding me?!

00:20:57.050 --> 00:20:57.900
Damn...

00:21:00.190 --> 00:21:00.960
To first!

00:21:00.960 --> 00:21:02.280
Shut up!

00:21:03.990 --> 00:21:04.830
Safe!

00:21:09.080 --> 00:21:11.330
Wh-What is he doing?

00:21:14.960 --> 00:21:16.500
Hey, Shigeno!

00:21:16.500 --> 00:21:17.670
What's wrong?

00:21:17.670 --> 00:21:18.830
Calm down.

00:21:20.950 --> 00:21:22.590
Shigeno?

00:21:23.110 --> 00:21:27.260
Now hitting: number 32, Chavez!

00:21:28.030 --> 00:21:30.470
I just need to get them out, right?

00:21:30.470 --> 00:21:32.470
Then that's what I'll do!

00:21:34.540 --> 00:21:35.360
Ball!

00:21:37.370 --> 00:21:38.190
Ball!

00:21:38.190 --> 00:21:39.430
Ball two.

00:21:41.780 --> 00:21:43.440
It's not working...

00:21:51.250 --> 00:21:52.260
What are you doing?

00:21:52.260 --> 00:21:52.930
Go home!

00:21:52.930 --> 00:21:54.480
This is your fault!

00:21:54.480 --> 00:21:55.970
You've got to be kidding me!

00:21:55.970 --> 00:21:57.740
You yellow-belly!

00:21:59.730 --> 00:22:02.930
If you don't like what I said, then pull through this situation,

00:22:02.930 --> 00:22:07.180
you coward.

00:22:53.470 --> 00:22:59.350
usubeni hikaru sora kono hoshi wa nemuranai

00:22:53.470 --> 00:22:59.350
The sky glows a faint red, illuminated by a star that never sleeps.

00:22:59.350 --> 00:23:04.730
yoake wa zutto yorisou

00:22:59.350 --> 00:23:04.730
The dawn will forever creep up on us.

00:23:05.110 --> 00:23:10.990
kimi ga doko ni ite mo nani kangaeteitemo

00:23:05.110 --> 00:23:10.990
No matter where you are, or what you're thinking,

00:23:10.990 --> 00:23:15.790
mawaru hoshi chihyou wa hitotsu dake

00:23:10.990 --> 00:23:15.790
there's only earth. One spinning planet.

00:23:16.540 --> 00:23:22.380
ikuoku mo aru yume wo mitetayo

00:23:16.540 --> 00:23:22.380
I had dreams, hundreds of millions of dreams.

00:23:22.380 --> 00:23:28.260
tsukamu kibou mitsuketa ne

00:23:22.380 --> 00:23:28.260
I finally found the hope I could hold on to.

00:23:28.260 --> 00:23:34.050
ikuoku no yoru kimi to nagameta

00:23:28.260 --> 00:23:34.050
The sky you and I gazed up at for hundreds of millions of nights

00:23:34.050 --> 00:23:39.520
sora mo tsunagatteiru

00:23:34.050 --> 00:23:39.520
is always connected wherever we are.

00:23:39.520 --> 00:23:45.980
zutto miteru dake no anohi no akogare no tame ni

00:23:39.520 --> 00:23:45.980
For the inspiration that I never lose sight of,

00:23:45.980 --> 00:23:51.240
shinjite tsuzuketa omoi wo

00:23:45.980 --> 00:23:54.700
I'll shape my life-long feelings into something tangible.

00:23:51.240 --> 00:23:54.700
zettai katachi ni suru

00:23:54.700 --> 00:23:57.160
boku to yakusoku shita

00:23:54.700 --> 00:24:03.540
The place where you and I made the promise calls out to you.

00:23:57.160 --> 00:24:03.540
ano basho ga kimi wo yobuyo

00:24:03.630 --> 00:24:07.380
sotto

00:24:03.630 --> 00:24:07.380
It gently calls out to you.

00:24:10.210 --> 00:24:15.550
Preview

00:24:10.210 --> 00:24:15.550
Preview

00:24:11.550 --> 00:24:13.800
No matter how much I pitch, I just can't get it right.

00:24:13.800 --> 00:24:16.220
What's going on with me?

00:24:17.140 --> 00:24:18.890
Are you kidding?

00:24:18.890 --> 00:24:21.430
I'll make it through this with my willpower!

00:24:22.180 --> 00:24:25.190
Next time on Major: The Southpaw in Distress!

00:24:25.190 --> 00:24:27.560
Run toward the stage of your dreams!

00:24:25.190 --> 00:24:30.570
Next Time

00:24:25.190 --> 00:24:30.570
Next Time

00:24:25.190 --> 00:24:30.570
The Southpaw in Distress

00:24:25.190 --> 00:24:30.570
The Southpaw in Distress
